{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   COLOUR MACRO — LOCAL STAND-IN, REPLACED AT HANDOFF

   Foster's site already has this macro; the gallery row imports it exactly as
   their existing rows do (see "predefined row reference.twig"). This file exists
   only so the row renders in the local harness. At handoff it is DELETED and
   Foster's real _macros/color.twig takes over.

   That is why the row template must never hardcode colour classes: the whole
   point of going through the macro is that their implementation wins in
   production without the row changing.

   The class names below use the brand tokens declared in src/css/gallery.css
   (@theme), so light/dark themes resolve to real palette values locally.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}

{% macro bgColor(theme) %}{{ theme == 'dark' ? 'bg-sabin-dark-gray' : 'bg-sabin-off-white' }}{% endmacro %}

{% macro textColor(theme) %}{{ theme == 'dark' ? 'text-sabin-off-white' : 'text-sabin-dark-gray' }}{% endmacro %}

{# The colour a tile sits on, so media carrying transparency never shows through
   to whatever is behind the row. #}
{% macro tileBgColor(theme) %}{{ theme == 'dark' ? 'bg-[#3a3a3a]' : 'bg-sabin-light-gray' }}{% endmacro %}
